// FIRST DRAFT (phase 6): rewrite or sign off. Voice: docs/voice.md. Flags: docs/story-drafts.md.
// The freed thrall's first night (docs/tech-spec.md §72): Kormak was freed the same day you were, and has no kin this side of the sea, so he lives with yours.
Tucked into Ulf's letter is a strip of birch bark with no words on it, only a picture cut with a knife point: a long table, a stamp, and a woman behind it with her sleeves rolled up.
You know the hand. Kormak never learned his runes on the jarl's farm, and never saw the point of learning them after. He draws.
Under the table he's cut a sun, low on the edge of the bark, with rays like a hedgehog's. He always said you were up before it.
* [Draw him one back.]
  # fx: flag kormak_drawn
  You draw the long hall, the forty cots and the fire nobody feeds. Then, because he'll like it, a very small Skögul eating a very large apple.
* [Write to him anyway.]
  # fx: flag kormak_written
  You write it out in big plain runes, so your mother can read it to him: the gate, the queue, the stamp. At the end you write that you're still up before the sun, and that nobody here has noticed.
- The raven takes it, and the drawing of the hedgehog sun stays propped against your cot.
-> END
